description: Pin top-of-screen chrome and notifications with sticky or fixed top 0
alwaysApply: true
---

# Sticky top chrome and notifications

Anything that sits at the **top of the screen** stays pinned there.

- Use `position: sticky; top: 0` (or `position: fixed; top: 0`) for headers, banners, and notifications.
- Toasts and login alerts (Sonner) stay at the **top**. Keep enter/leave animation. Do not park them in `<main>` as in-flow copy.
- Do not invent a reserved gap, frost slab, or `env(safe-area-inset-*)` pad to “make room” for top chrome.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — notification scrolls away with page content
<main>
  <div>Welcome back!</div>
  <Outlet />
</main>

// ✅ GOOD — pinned top toast
<Toaster position="top-right" />
<header className="sticky top-0 z-40">…</header>
```
